WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.805
Mastery Starter 4.0.

00:00:02.805 --> 00:00:04.125
New to Yield?

00:00:04.125 --> 00:00:05.185
Start here.

00:00:05.185 --> 00:00:07.272
In about ten minutes, you'll go from

00:00:07.272 --> 00:00:08.965
zero to ready for this module.

00:00:10.265 --> 00:00:12.405
Every yield is payment for a risk.

00:00:12.405 --> 00:00:14.890
Staking pays you to secure a network,

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.898
lending pays for borrower demand, farms often

00:00:17.898 --> 00:00:20.029
pay in newly printed tokens.

00:00:20.029 --> 00:00:21.855
This module teaches you to see

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.739
what each yield really pays for.

00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:28.549
APY: yearly return including compounding.

00:00:28.549 --> 00:00:32.089
Emissions: new reward tokens printed by a protocol.

00:00:32.089 --> 00:00:35.439
Staking: locking tokens to help secure a network.

00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:39.704
LST: a token representing staked assets.

00:00:39.704 --> 00:00:43.838
RWA: a token representing a real-world asset.

00:00:45.137 --> 00:00:46.772
Modules 0–3.

00:00:48.072 --> 00:00:51.795
Take any advertised APY and split it into base

00:00:51.795 --> 00:00:56.152
yield vs incentives using the protocol's own dashboard.

00:00:57.452 --> 00:01:00.062
Beginner: Tells base yield from emissions.

00:01:00.062 --> 00:01:02.976
Practitioner: Compares vaults vs DIY

00:01:02.976 --> 00:01:06.032
and prices points/airdrops as bets.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.920
Master: Builds yield from durable sources:

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.547
lending, staking, savings rates, tokenized treasuries.

00:01:13.847 --> 00:01:16.219
You've mastered this module when you can

00:01:16.219 --> 00:01:18.301
name the source and the risk behind

00:01:18.301 --> 00:01:19.805
any yield in one sentence.

00:01:21.106 --> 00:01:23.621
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:23.621 --> 00:01:25.906
Next up, Lesson 4.1: Yield

00:01:25.906 --> 00:01:28.698
farming: base yield vs emissions.
